// Authored relations — the editorial layer of the relations lens.
// Every pair carries tension/friction/harmony weights (relative, normalized in code) and a WHY in
// the project's voice. Coverage is 370 pairs: all 190 among the 20 states, plus all 180 between a
// state and one of the 9 non-state actors, so the derived fallback in relations-model.ts decides
// none of the 560 readings any constellation asks for (verified, not assumed).
//
// Actor↔actor pairs are deliberately absent. A constellation is drawn FROM a state, so it only
// ever asks how a member relates to that state — never how two actors relate to each other. See
// MEMBERS vs STATES in relations-model.ts.
// Interpretive judgment, not a clinical claim — same plan as `power`: empirical later.
//
// CURRENCY: written against the situation as of September 2026, and several pairs turn on events
// from the first half of that year — the February–June US/Israel–Iran war and its June
// memorandum, the 2026 Lebanon war and the Washington disarmament framework, the Gaza transition
// under UNSCR 2803, Syria under al-Sharaa, and the Riyadh–Abu Dhabi split. Those are the rows
// most likely to age; revisit them first.

// LABEL SWAP (direct feedback, not a naming preference — matches relations-model.ts's POLE_HE,
// Chrome.tsx's POLE, and engine.ts's POLE_HE): the FIELD names below (t/f, "tension"/"friction")
// and every value assigned to them are UNCHANGED — only the Hebrew word each one displays as was
// wrong. Corrected: `t` is open/direct confrontation — adversarial pressure, shadow wars, proxies
// — and displays as חיכוך. `f` is day-to-day grinding WITHOUT direct enmity, opposing interests
// short of confrontation — and displays as מתח. (The TS identifiers "tension"/"friction" are NOT
// translations of the Hebrew words they now display as — see each consumer's own comment.)
export interface AuthoredRelation {
  pair: [string, string]
  t: number // tension  → displays as חיכוך — adversarial pressure, direct confrontation
  f: number // friction → displays as מתח   — day-to-day grinding without enmity
  h: number // harmony  (הרמוניה) — alignment and cooperation
  why: string
}

